{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1383375-combat-rules-help-please","id":1383375,"title":"Combat Rules Help Please","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-23T08:40:50-07:00","id":1383375,"title":"Combat Rules Help Please","content":"My group and I are getting in the groove of playing 2nd Ed with the goal of eventually releasing our games as a podcast, but we got caught up on the combat rules recently, and I want to make sure our current interpretation is correct. Since there is no example in the book its not 100% clear. Where we are getting caught up is the combat rules seem to vary slightly from the base rules. Most tests you have to have successes = difficulty to succeed (Origin, pg 63 &quot;&quot;...vault a difficulty 2 gap between buildings, she must roll at least 2 successes to buy off the difficulty and succeed.&quot;) But for combat it seems to be difficulty+1 (Origin pg 116, 3rd paragraph under Attacking &quot;If you roll enough success to <b>exceed</b> their Defense, your attack succeeds.&quot;)<br /> <br /> this is the example I posted in our discord server and I want to make sure that I am correct in my interpretation. Thank you all for the help!<br /> <br /> Betty the Scion of Bast is battling bad boys Bill, Bob, and Barry.<br /> <br /> Bill swings for Betty with his bat.<br /> <br /> Betty rolls her defense pool of 5 and gets 3 successes, her defense is now 4 (1 base+ 3 success)<br /> <br /> Bill rolls a 3 successes. That does not <b>exceed</b> her defense of 4 so Bill misses badly.<br /> <br /> Bob has a boomerang, and throws it at Betty. Her defense is still 4 because she has not had a turn yet. He rolls a 4. His roll does not <b>exceed</b> her defense of 4 so his attack has no effect<br /> <br /> Barry is up next and he has a battle axe. He rolls a 5. Betty still has a defense of 4 because she has not had a turn yet. Barry's battle axe barrage barely <b>exceeds</b> Betty's defense of 4 so he succeeds. (Here is the part where I need clarification but I'm fairly certain this is correct, once I get on the fourms I will be sure). He would like to Inflict Damage on Betty. Betty is wearing Soft Armor 1. Barry doesn't have enough successes to overcome this Soft Armor so his attack connects but bounces off of Betty's biker jacket.<br /> <br /> Betty goes! Betty is more worried about Barry and his battle axe so she tries to stab him with her bowie knife. Barry has a defense of 3. Betty rolls a 7. Her attack <b>exceeds</b> his defense of 3. Barry is not wearing armor. So Betty has a net of 3 successes to spend on stunts (Def 3 +1 for exceed= 4-7=3 net) She can Inflict Damage for (0+Barry's soft armor of 0=0) leaving her with 3 to spend on other stunts. Betty's bowie knife is a relic, with the brutal tag. She can buy the Critical Strike stunt for 1 less success so it would only cost her 3. She buys Critical to deal an additional Injury Condition to Barry. Barry only had 2 health, so Betty's blade bifurcates Barry's bicep and he is now Taken Out<br /> <br /> Bill see's Barry's blody body and gets out his baretta. Betty rolls her defense pool and gets 5 successes! Her defense is now 6 (1 base + 5 successes) Bill squeezes off a shot and gets 7 successes (lucky Bill!) This exceeds Betty's defense pool of 6 so he succeeds. Bill's barretta is Piercing, so he ignores 2 points of Soft Armor. He spends 0 successes to Inflict Damage on Betty (0+1 for soft armor [ignored by piercing]=0) and Betty takes a Lethal Injury condition (Ouch!)<br /> <br /> if Betty had Bullet Proof armor, she would not have taken an injury condition because her armor would have ignored the piercing quality of the weapon<br /> <br /> If you don't want to inflict damage you could spend successes over what's required to exceed their defense on other stunts. Say you can't get through someones incredible magic armor. You could still do Knock Down/Trip (1 success) for example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26109-snowtiefling","name":"SnowTiefling","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:03:25-07:00","id":1383378,"title":"","content":"The wording slightly earlier, in the summary, is better where they say &quot;overcome the target's Defense.&quot; They mean roll enough successes to meat the Defense difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:27:03-07:00","id":1383383,"title":"","content":"You need only the successes equal to the Defense to hit (you don\u2019t need to exceed it), BUT hit does not mean cause injury (as you pointed). Cause injury is a stunt that can cost 0 if the target is not wearing any armor, otherwise it costs the target soft armor value. If the attack hit but there are no success enough to cause injury (or otherwise exceeding successes) you can add other stunts.<br /> <br /> Using your example, Barry first attack had 5 successes, so he could beat the Defense (using 4 successes) and the spare success (1) beat the soft armor, causing the injury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:28:08-07:00","id":1383384,"title":"","content":"In terms of making combat rolls, you need to meet their difficulty to hit. Initially, the Inflict Injury stunt cost 1 success, which is probably why they stated you needed to exceed the defense.<br /> <br /> With the Inflict Injury Stunt costing 0 successes, now you just need to meet the difficulty to hit and injure a foe. I think this was changed because it was objectively worse to meet someone's defense than to miss them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T18:14:54-07:00","id":1383486,"title":"","content":"Thank you all very much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This was a big help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26109-snowtiefling","name":"SnowTiefling","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}